---
import {experimentFields, experimentMethods, defaultExperiment, createExperimentOutline} from '../data/experiment-directions';
import '../styles/experiment-planner.css';
const outline = createExperimentOutline(defaultExperiment.field, defaultExperiment.method, defaultExperiment.starter);
---
<section class='experiment-planner' id='experiment' data-experiment-planner data-experiment-field={outline.field.id} data-experiment-method={outline.method.id}>
 <div class='section-heading'><h2>Give the question<br/><em>a way forward.</em></h2><p>A small research outline. Choose what you need to learn, a method that fits, and the observation that could change your next decision.</p></div>
 <form class='experiment-controls' data-experiment-controls hidden>
  <div class='experiment-starting-point'>
   <label for='experiment-field'>Where would you begin?<select id='experiment-field' name='field' data-experiment-field-control>{experimentFields.map(field=><option value={field.id} selected={field.id===outline.field.id}>{field.name}</option>)}</select></label>
   <label for='experiment-starter'>A question to start with<select id='experiment-starter' name='starter' data-experiment-starter>{outline.field.starters.map((question,index)=><option value={index} selected={index===outline.starter}>{question}</option>)}</select></label>
  </div>
  <label class='experiment-question-control' for='experiment-question'>Or put the question in your own words<textarea id='experiment-question' name='question' maxlength='1000' rows='3' data-experiment-question placeholder={outline.question} aria-describedby='experiment-question-note'></textarea><span id='experiment-question-note'>Keep it specific and use non-sensitive information. Your words stay in this page unless you choose to copy, save or continue.</span></label>
  <fieldset class='experiment-methods'><legend>How could you learn?</legend><div>{experimentMethods.map(method=><label><input type='radio' name='method' value={method.id} checked={method.id===outline.method.id} data-experiment-method-control/><span><strong>{method.name}</strong><span>{method.purpose}</span></span></label>)}</div></fieldset>
 </form>
 <div class='experiment-connection' aria-hidden='true'><svg viewBox='0 0 720 100' preserveAspectRatio='none'><path class='experiment-connection-line' d='M48 50 C150 50 200 50 360 50 C520 50 570 50 672 50'/><circle class='experiment-node experiment-node-question' cx='48' cy='50' r='9'/><circle class='experiment-node experiment-node-method' cx='360' cy='50' r='9'/><circle class='experiment-node experiment-node-observation' cx='672' cy='50' r='9'/></svg><span>A question</span><span>A way to learn</span><span>A next decision</span></div>
 <div class='experiment-outline' data-experiment-outline>
  <article class='experiment-question-panel'><span class='experiment-panel-label'>Question</span><h3 data-experiment-question-preview>{outline.question}</h3><p class='experiment-context' data-experiment-context>{outline.field.context}</p><div class='experiment-inputs'><h4>Start with</h4><ul data-experiment-inputs>{outline.inputs.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul></div><p class='experiment-scope'>A planning aid for a bounded investigation. Use invented, public or appropriately permitted information.</p></article>
  <article class='experiment-method-panel'><span class='experiment-panel-label'>Method</span><h3 data-experiment-method-name>{outline.method.name}</h3><p data-experiment-purpose>{outline.method.purpose}</p><div><h4>Prepare</h4><p data-experiment-preparation>{outline.method.preparation}</p></div><div><h4>Try</h4><p data-experiment-activity>{outline.method.activity}</p></div></article>
  <article class='experiment-observation-panel'><span class='experiment-panel-label'>Observation</span><h3>Notice what<br/>changes the view.</h3><div><h4>Watch for</h4><ul data-experiment-observations>{outline.observations.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul></div><div class='experiment-limit'><h4>What this cannot establish</h4><p data-experiment-limit>{outline.method.limit}</p></div><div class='experiment-decision'><h4>Next decision</h4><p data-experiment-decision>{outline.decision}</p></div></article>
 </div>
 <div class='experiment-actions' data-experiment-actions hidden><button class='experiment-continue' type='button' data-experiment-continue>Continue with this outline</button><div><button type='button' data-experiment-copy>Copy outline</button><button type='button' data-experiment-download>Save as text</button><button type='button' data-experiment-share>Copy a link</button><button type='button' data-experiment-reset>Start again</button></div></div>
 <p class='experiment-status' role='status' aria-live='polite' data-experiment-status></p>
 <div class='experiment-copy-fallback' data-experiment-copy-fallback hidden><label for='experiment-copy-text' data-experiment-copy-label>Your outline</label><textarea id='experiment-copy-text' readonly rows='8' data-experiment-copy-text></textarea><p>Select the text and copy it using your browser.</p></div>
 <div class='experiment-notes'><p data-experiment-share-note>Shared links contain the field, method and starter question. They never contain your custom question. Continuing opens an inquiry you can review and edit before sending.</p><a class='inline-link' data-experiment-inquiry href='/contact?project=nrth-labs'>Open a blank NRTH Labs inquiry</a></div>
 <div class='experiment-method-library'><h3>Different methods.<br/>Different kinds of evidence.</h3><p class='experiment-library-intro'>A better outline makes the limits as clear as the ambition. Compare the methods before choosing what to try.</p>{experimentMethods.map(method=><details><summary>{method.name}</summary><div><p>{method.purpose}</p><h4>What it asks of you</h4><p>{method.preparation}</p><h4>What it cannot establish</h4><p>{method.limit}</p></div></details>)}</div>
</section>
<script>import '../scripts/experiment-planner';</script>
